00:01:51.389 --> 00:01:53.359
events of The Rickshank Redemption.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:58.249
Democratic elections are being held for the
first time in the wake up of the uh, dissolution

00:01:58.249 --> 00:01:59.640
of the council of Ricks.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.640
Hold on, hold on, *gun zapping* AHHH!

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.759
The world building in this episode is freaking
amazing, especially in how it cleverly mirrors

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:12.810
our current political climate - from a news
organization that’s one “N” away from

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:16.840
“CNN” that trivializes dissent in order
to maintain the status quo,

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.400
Anyway so yea, the suspect says that citadel is a lie, built on lies

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.740
and some other s***.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.980
I say appreciate the life you have, because it can always be worse.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:31.360
to an inner city devastated by drugs and guns, to a Hogwarts that teaches the disenfranchised Mortys to

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.040
accept their lot in life.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.560
This is a great adventure

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.140
This is a great adventure

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:41.000
This is definitely one of the harder narratives
to follow, and certainly more complex than

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.520
your traditional episode.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.860
So I want to lay out the many subplots as
follows:

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.890
Evil Morty comes to power on a platform of
unity and change, before revealing his grander,

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.330
and more totalitarian intentions.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:58.060
In an allusion to Training Day, A fresh out
of the academy police Rick has to join a crooked

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:03.060
cop Morty and confront the corrupt underbelly
of the Citadel where he is forced to confront

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.320
his ideals, and abandon them.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:10.620
It seems reminiscent of the ending of "L.A. Confidential",
where an idealistic cop has to break the rules

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.660
and kill his superior- undermining the same
justice system he thought he was protecting.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:20.860
A group of orphaned Mortys set off for adventure
a la "Stand By Me," before sending their hopes

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.300
and dreams into the literal trash.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.600
Garbage dump. Stand *burp* back.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.560
A Rick is passed over for a promotion and
realizes he’s wasted his life on an assembly

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.400
line.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.260
He revolts, but his triumph is quickly ruined
by the powers that be.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:42.370
In all of these cases, we see any kind of
political or personal optimism for change

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:45.490
crushed by a cruel and indifferent reality.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:49.260
This episode really builds off the themes
that we talked about earlier in Rickmancing

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.300
the Stone.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:55.480
Specifically, alienation, or the way modern
society estranges us from the world and our

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.819
peers, making us all dead inside.

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:02.720
In the case of Rickmancing the Stone the creature
comforts of society turn the exciting world

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.240
of the apocalypse into a domestic nightmare.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:10.260
Now, we see many versions of the smartest
man in the universe reduced to the drudgery

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.400
of modern life.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.180
And mixed in, we see signs of a deeply divided
society.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:20.600
Candidate Morty,  the number of displaced Mortys is soaring while Rick satisfaction levels are plummeting.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.120
And the divide between the two groups has never been whiter.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.440
Solve that one real quick.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.980
But as Evil Morty suggests- this is a distraction.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.800
The citadel's problem isn't homeless Mortys or outraged Ricks,

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.800
The citadel's problem is the Ricks and Mortys feeding on the citadels death.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.960
The real divide? -- the Rich vs. The Working
Class.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.980
I don't see a divide between Ricks and Mortys the division I see,

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:46.480
is between the Ricks and Mortys that like the citadel divided, and the rest of us.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:51.340
What’s interesting is that, despite the
apparent ruling class of Ricks, everyone is

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.060
a victim 
of alienation.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.700
They told us we were special because we were Ricks, but they stripped us of everything that make us unique

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.280
That doesn't sound like Rick work. You didn't come to the citadel to become a plumber, did you?

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.020
Even the cops are likened to just workers
on the assembly line of justice.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:08.720
We know how you feel,  we're working stiff Ricks just like you, but our assembly line is justice.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.540
But in addition to being victims of those
individuals in power, the Ricks are also victims

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:18.260
of an impenetrable system. And here’s where
my favorite part of the whole episode comes in.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.640
His name is Simple Rick, but he's no dummy.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:26.480
He realized long ago that the greatest thing he'd ever create was his daughter.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.560
I love daddy!

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.540
We captured that moment, we run it on a loop for Simple Rick's mind.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.680
And the chemical that makes his brain secrete goes into every

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.220
Simple Rick Simple Wafers Wafer Cookie

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.720
Come home to the impossible flavor of your own completion.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.740
Come home to Simple Ricks.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:47.160
This gets at a really smart question, tackled
by a lot of different philosophers.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:52.040
But I’ll summarize the issue as this: Is
our escape from the alienation of modern life

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:56.780
just strengthening the foundations of the
system that drives that alienation?

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:01.580
Simple Rick follows what I’ll call the ‘Ron
Swanson” trope - someone who fights our

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:06.419
fast-paced world by slowing down, working
with their hands, and spending time with the

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:07.419
family.

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:12.880
In a world that crams us in cubicles and hunches
us over assembly lines, our only respite is

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.020
the "simple life.”

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:18.830
Running away from the urban clamor, living
off the land, learning a trade like woodworking,

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:21.250
reconnecting with your family, etc.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:25.360
Not surprisingly, this kind of idea gained
prevalence as the world was industrializing,

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.240
and subsequently corporatized.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.110
We saw the rise of organizations like the
boy scouts and the establishment of national

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:34.620
parks - where you could practice not being
crammed in a city.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.430
But it could be argued that this escape to
the simple life, whether in the form of nature,

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:44.110
or family, or woodworking, is not in fact
retreating from the system, but an essential

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:45.960
part of its functioning.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:51.570
We can view the Simple Rick wafers “brand”
as a kind of fantasy that reinforces the system.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.919
Ricks show up for work because they know they
can go home and allegedly unplug from the

00:06:55.919 --> 00:07:00.960
system with the distilled essence of simplicity,
even though this “unplugging” comes in

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:07.180
commodity form - one that requires, you know,
money that you have to work for at an assembly line.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:11.480
And we’ve all seen enough cereal commercials
to know that advertisers love selling us a

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:16.220
kind of “pure, wholesome” family who actually eats meals together without screaming at each other

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:21.680
Sociologist George Ritzer says that our enchantment
with, and disenchantment from, the modern

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.760
world are not so easy to distinguish from
each other.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.990
He even says they exist in a reciprocal relation.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:32.740
In other words, the fantasy of unplugging
with some Simple Rick Wafers further entrenches

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:36.080
you in the very system you want to unplug
from.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.620
But it gets even more devious.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:43.900
As one Rick decides he’s had enough, he
engages in an actual act of rebellion: killing

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.979
his boss, and trying to get a portal gun to
ACTUALLY escape the system.

00:07:47.979 --> 00:07:53.030
But instead of affecting change, his rebellion
is commodified in the form of the “simple

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.560
rick freedom wafer selects.”

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.980
Come home to the unique flavor of shattering the grand illusion.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:05.000
He endlessly lives the joy of rebellion, while
the system distills this joy in a consumable

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:05.520
form.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.980
Freedom from the system entraps you in the
system.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:13.420
Ritzer goes on to say that “Fantasies draw
people into the new means of consumption,

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:17.440
and those fantasies can be rationalized in
order to further draw people in.”

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:21.880
And this, for me, makes this the darkest episode
of the season yet.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:27.639
The message seems to be - In the terrifying
political reality that is 2017 - the best

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:30.889
we can hope for is the illusion of making
a difference.

00:08:30.889 --> 00:08:34.199
If you don’t believe me, remember the orphan
Morty’s plot.

00:08:34.199 --> 00:08:38.520
They go on a coming of age adventure, trying
to escape their terrible orphan existence

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:41.020
and their bondage to some future Rick.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:46.580
But the wish portal turns out to be a garbage
portal - the system turns wishes into literal

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.860
trash.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:53.340
Slick Morty sacrifices himself to wish for
a better world, and it happens - sort of.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.340
Holy crap. Slicks wish came true.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:59.440
I don’t think we’re meant to believe that
his sacrifice magically made things better

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:03.820
- especially because the change promised was
just a ploy by Evil Morty.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:08.000
The subplot has no actual bearing on the overall
narrative, it only seems to exist for the

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.301
writers to show us the naive ideas of these
children - that Slick Morty’s sacrifice

00:09:12.301 --> 00:09:14.240
could have changed something.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.410
Nothing they did mattered, but they get to
believe it did, just like our revolting Rick.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.070
So what do we make of Evil Morty?

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:25.800
He sold a kind of class consciousness to the
Ricks and Mortys of the citadel - that Ricks

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.540
and Mortys should join together to make a
better world against the ruling elite.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.780
But with the brutal purge of his political
opponents, it seems like this was nothing

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:36.899
more than lip service as a means to power.

00:09:36.899 --> 00:09:40.770
But hey- could we really expect any kind of
real progress from this show?

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:45.490
There is just SO much going on this episode
that we haven’t touched on - like Is there

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:49.750
some connection between this Latin phrase
on the chalkboard and Evil Morty’s view

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.290
of how society functions?

